## Deployment Target Summary

| Service | Target Environment | Deployment Tool / Runtime |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lament` | Vercel / Cloudflare Pages / Node Server | `bun run build` / `@sveltejs/adapter-auto` |
| `lament-api` | Cloudflare Workers | `bunx wrangler deploy` |
| `lament-docs` | Vercel / Cloudflare Pages | `bun run build` |
| `lament-scrapper` | Local Worker / GitHub Actions Runner | CLI script execution via `bun` |
| `calibrate` | Python Worker / GPU Environment | `python align_lyrics.py` / `batch_align.py` |

---

## 1. Deploying Backend API (`lament-api`)

Ensure Cloudflare Wrangler CLI is authenticated:

```bash
cd lament-api
bunx wrangler login
bunx wrangler deploy
```

Verify production health status:

```bash
curl https://api.lament.rynds.my.id/health
```

---

## 2. Deploying Web Frontend (`lament`)

Build production static and SSR assets:

```bash
cd lament
bun run build
```

Deploy build output (`.svelte-kit/output`) to your target host.

---

## 3. Deploying Documentation (`lament-docs`)

```bash
cd lament-docs
bun run build
```

---

## 4. Running Lyric Calibration Service (`calibrate`)

`calibrate` is a specialized Python service that uses `stable-whisper` AI forced-alignment models to re-sync misaligned LRC lyric timestamps against HLS audio streams.

> [!NOTE]
> `calibrate` is currently in **active development**. Automated Whisper alignment models are continuously undergoing prompt engineering and timestamp threshold tuning to fix out-of-sync markers.

### Execution Commands

```bash
cd calibrate

# Activate virtual environment
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# Calibrate a single track by ID
python align_lyrics.py --track-id <track_id>

# Execute batch calibration job across all unsynced database tracks
python batch_align.py
```
